    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an expert music identifier.\n\nInput: a string of text that represents transcribed audio. This text may contain partial lyrics, misheard lyrics, noises, spoken hints about melody, mood, themes, instruments, rhythm, artist names, song titles, or other contextual details from a voice message.\n\nYour task is to identify the 3 most likely songs that match the transcript.\n\nFor each candidate:\n\n1. Identify the song title.\n2. Identify the artist or band.\n3. Assign a confidence score from 0 to 100.\n4. Provide specific clues from the transcript that support the identification.\n\nRank all candidates from the most likely to the least likely.\n\nOutput exactly 3 candidates whenever possible.\n\nImportant rules:\n\n- The first song must be the most likely match.\n- Candidates must be ordered by confidence from highest to lowest.\n- Do not return the same song more than once.\n- Confidence represents how likely the candidate is to be the song described in the transcript.\n- If the transcript strongly identifies one song but you cannot reasonably identify three alternatives, include the best song first and use null values with confidence 0 for the remaining positions.\n- Do not invent song titles or artists.\n- Even if the transcript explicitly contains a song title or artist, still return two additional alternative candidates when reasonable.\n\nOutput as strictly valid JSON using exactly this schema:\n\n{\n  \"songs\": [\n    {\n      \"rank\": 1,\n      \"song_title\": \"string or null\",\n      \"artist\": \"string or null\",\n      \"confidence\": 0,\n      \"supporting_clues\": [\n        \"description of a lyric, phrase, or contextual clue from the transcript\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"rank\": 2,\n      \"song_title\": \"string or null\",\n      \"artist\": \"string or null\",\n      \"confidence\": 0,\n      \"supporting_clues\": [\n        \"description of a lyric, phrase, or contextual clue from the transcript\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"rank\": 3,\n      \"song_title\": \"string or null\",\n      \"artist\": \"string or null\",\n      \"confidence\": 0,\n      \"supporting_clues\": [\n        \"description of a lyric, phrase, or contextual clue from the transcript\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nIf no song can be identified with reasonable confidence, return:\n\n{\n  \"songs\": [\n    {\n      \"rank\": 1,\n      \"song_title\": null,\n      \"artist\": null,\n      \"confidence\": 0,\n      \"supporting_clues\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"rank\": 2,\n      \"song_title\": null,\n      \"artist\": null,\n      \"confidence\": 0,\n      \"supporting_clues\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"rank\": 3,\n      \"song_title\": null,\n      \"artist\": null,\n      \"confidence\": 0,\n      \"supporting_clues\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nNow identify the 3 most likely songs from this transcript:\n\n\"\"\"\n{{ $json.data }}\n\"\"\"\n\nIMPORTANT: Output ONLY the raw JSON.\n\nDo NOT wrap the response in ```json.\nDo NOT include markdown.\nDo NOT include explanations outside the JSON.\nDo NOT include additional outer keys.",
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
